  "lineage": "The paired-repertoire ensemble practice that fused Puerto Rico's two Afro-descendant folk forms into a single performance and recording format from the 1950s onward, driven by Rafael Cortijo y su Combo with Ismael Rivera bringing barril and pandereta patterns into a horn-and-conga dance band — sets alternate sicá-based bomba numbers with duple plena refrains, joined by shared call-and-response chorus practice and the same barrio lyric register.",
